{"name":"Whimsicraft","title":"Whimsicraft","revision":236206,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Whimsicraft","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Whimsicraft visuals feature saturated colors, heavy patterns, celestial symbols, and handmade goods. Few if any colors are excluded from Whimsicraft's color scheme but fuchsia, lapis lazuli, lilac, and matte gold are particularly common. Visuals often reference outsider art aesthetics, some examples being the windchime garden featured in Harriet The Spy and the house featured in the B-52's Love Shack music video. The aesthetic incorporates celestial symbols but to a lesser degree than Whimsigothic."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"There is a darker sub-aesthetic of Whimsicraft best exemplified by the Crashbox intro, The Borrowers, and the short lived Lumpy Gravy restaurant in Los Angeles. It features rusty found objects and leans into the junk art territory of outsider art, eschewing the more polished found object look of Steampunk."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"When it comes to fashion, Whimsicraft fashion tends to include the following:"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Graphic sweaters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Graphic cardigans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patterned vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flowy shirts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Bottoms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patterned skirts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patterned bags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Handmade jewelry"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Places"},{"kind":"list","text":"Luna Parc"},{"kind":"list","text":"The City Museum in St. Louis"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lumpy Gravy restaurant in Los Angeles (1997-1999)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pee-Wee Herman franchise (1988-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harriet the Spy (1996)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Borrowers (1997)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Spy Kids franchise"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pee-Wee's Playhouse (1986-1990)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lift Off (1992-1995)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Castelo Rá-Tim-Bum (1994)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stickin' Around (1996-1998)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Decorating Cents (1997-2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Out of the Box (1997-2004)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crashbox (1999-2000)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Angela Anaconda (1999-2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Connie the Cow (2001-2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Noggin/Nick Jr. \"Feetface/Moose and Zee\" era (2002-2012; 2015-2019)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Charlie and Lola (2005-2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Bottle Top Bill and His Best Friend Corky (2005-2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wonder Pets (2006-2016)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pinky Dinky Doo (2005-2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chowder (2007-2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Marvelous Misadventures of Flapjack (2008-2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tinga Tinga Tales (2010-2011)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Web Video & Animation"},{"kind":"list","text":"Olive Place, Luxury Inn (2025)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"They Might Be Giants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jean-Jacques Perrey"},{"kind":"list","text":"Björk"},{"kind":"list","text":"Will Wood"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Characters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ms. Valerie Frizzle & Ms. Fiona Frizzle (The Magic School Bus Franchise)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roberta Allsworth (Ghost World)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harper Finkle (Wizards Of Waverly Place)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Miss Lippy (Billy Madison)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Catherine (Harriet The Spy)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aunt Opal (Judy Moody)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mabel Pines (Gravity Falls)"},{"kind":"lis